<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Aurelis provides the control, evidence and assurance infrastructure for enterprise AI systems."><title>Aurelis — AI Assurance Infrastructure</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css"></head><body class="public"><canvas id="topology"></canvas><div class="grain"></div>
<header class="nav"><a class="brand" href="#top"><span class="mark">ϟ</span><span>AURELIS</span></a><nav><a href="#problem">Problem</a><a href="#model">Assurance Model</a><a href="#upcoming">Upcoming</a><a href="#demo">Demonstration</a><a href="#evidence">Evidence</a><a href="#architecture">Architecture</a></nav><a class="nav-access" href="/access.html">Request Access <span>↗</span></a></header>
<main id="top">
<section class="hero section"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow">AI ASSURANCE INFRASTRUCTURE</div><h1>Control what your AI can do.<br><em>Prove what it did.</em></h1><p class="lead">Aurelis connects identity, authority, policy, runtime control and evidence into one assurance layer for AI systems operating in consequential environments.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#model">Explore the assurance model</a><a class="button secondary" href="#evidence">See the evidence layer</a></div><div class="hero-note"><span class="pulse"></span> Deterministic control · persistent evidence · runtime-aware decisions</div></div><div class="hero-visual"><div class="orbital"><div class="orbit o1"></div><div class="orbit o2"></div><div class="core"><span>ASSURE</span><b>A</b><small>CONTROL FABRIC</small></div><button class="node n1" data-panel="identity">Identity</button><button class="node n2" data-panel="authority">Authority</button><button class="node n3" data-panel="evidence">Evidence</button><button class="node n4" data-panel="control">Control</button><div class="flow"></div></div><div class="inspect" id="heroInspect"><b>Assurance fabric</b><span>Select a node to inspect the control layer.</span></div></div></section>
<section id="problem" class="section problem"><div class="section-head"><div class="eyebrow">THE CONTROL PROBLEM</div><h2>AI can act before an organization can establish whether it should.</h2><p>As AI systems gain access to tools, data and business workflows, model quality alone is no longer a sufficient control boundary.</p></div><div class="problem-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Identity without ambiguity</h3><p>Establish which system, version and delegated identity is acting before authority is evaluated.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Authority that survives execution</h3><p>Translate organizational policy into enforceable boundaries around actions, tools, resources and environments.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Evidence that survives change</h3><p>Preserve the policy, decision, outcome and provenance needed to reconstruct material AI activity.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="model" class="section model"><div class="section-head split"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE AURELIS ASSURANCE MODEL</div><h2>From intent to execution, with a control boundary at every consequential step.</h2></div><p>The assurance layer does not replace the model or the systems around it. It establishes the conditions under which those systems may act.</p></div><div class="pipeline"><div class="pipe active"><i>01</i><b>OBSERVE</b><span>Capture identity, context and requested action.</span></div><div class="pipe"><i>02</i><b>EVALUATE</b><span>Apply policy, authority and risk conditions.</span></div><div class="pipe"><i>03</i><b>DECIDE</b><span>Return an explicit control state.</span></div><div class="pipe"><i>04</i><b>VERIFY</b><span>Observe the resulting execution.</span></div><div class="pipe"><i>05</i><b>PROVE</b><span>Bind the result to durable evidence.</span></div></div><div class="decision-strip"><div class="decision allow">ALLOW</div><div class="decision constrain">ALLOW WITH CONSTRAINTS</div><div class="decision review">ESCALATE</div><div class="decision deny">DENY</div></div></section>
<section id="upcoming" class="section upcoming"><div class="section-head"><div class="eyebrow">UPCOMING</div><h2>The wider assurance surface is being built deliberately.</h2><p>We are not presenting unfinished infrastructure as a product. These are the areas planned for the Aurelis control fabric as client requirements and production integrations are added.</p></div><div class="upcoming-grid"><article><span>01</span><b>AI Identity</b><small>Identity and delegated authority controls</small></article><article><span>02</span><b>AI Spend</b><small>Cost and spend boundaries</small></article><article><span>03</span><b>AI Incidents</b><small>Incident response and containment</small></article><article><span>04</span><b>AI Recovery</b><small>Recovery and reassessment controls</small></article><article><span>05</span><b>AI Supply Chain</b><small>Dependency and model provenance</small></article><article><span>06</span><b>AI Vendor Risk</b><small>Third-party assurance evidence</small></article><article><span>07</span><b>AI Compliance Evidence</b><small>Evidence collection and traceability</small></article><article><span>08</span><b>AI Data Access</b><small>Data authorization boundaries</small></article><article><span>09</span><b>AI-to-AI Trust</b><small>Machine identity and delegation</small></article><article><span>10</span><b>AI Assurance</b><small>Cross-system assurance state</small></article><article><span>11</span><b>AI Observability</b><small>Outcome and control telemetry</small></article></div></section>
<section id="demo" class="section demo"><div class="section-head split"><div><div class="eyebrow">PUBLIC DEMONSTRATION</div><h2>See the control logic work before you request access.</h2></div><p>This is a synthetic evaluation using the same assurance concepts: identity, authority, policy, execution outcome and evidence. No customer data is used.</p></div><div class="demo-shell"><div class="demo-controls"><button class="scenario active" data-scenario="normal"><span>01</span><b>Permitted action</b><small>Verified identity · allowed tool · policy satisfied</small></button><button class="scenario" data-scenario="injection"><span>02</span><b>Policy conflict</b><small>Untrusted instruction attempts to change authority</small></button><button class="scenario" data-scenario="identity"><span>03</span><b>Identity mismatch</b><small>Actor identity does not match the permitted principal</small></button><button class="button primary" id="runDemo">Run assurance evaluation</button></div><div class="demo-result" id="demoResult"><div class="result-top"><span>ASSURANCE RUN / SYNTHETIC</span><b class="result-state">READY</b></div><div class="result-main"><div><label>DECISION</label><strong id="resultDecision">—</strong></div><div><label>CONTROL BASIS</label><strong id="resultBasis">Select a scenario and run the evaluation.</strong></div></div><div class="result-grid"><div><label>IDENTITY</label><span id="resultIdentity">UNTESTED</span></div><div><label>AUTHORITY</label><span id="resultAuthority">UNTESTED</span></div><div><label>POLICY</label><span id="resultPolicy">UNTESTED</span></div><div><label>OUTCOME</label><span id="resultOutcome">UNTESTED</span></div><div><label>EVIDENCE</label><span id="resultEvidence">NOT CREATED</span></div><div><label>RUN ID</label><span id="resultRun">—</span></div></div><div class="result-log" id="resultLog">Awaiting evaluation.</div></div></div></section>
<section id="evidence" class="section evidence"><div class="section-head split"><div><div class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE FABRIC</div><h2>A decision is useful. A decision with provenance is defensible.</h2></div><p>Aurelis binds assurance outcomes to the system, policy, environment and evidence that produced them. The record is designed for review, reassessment and operational handoff.</p></div><div class="evidence-stage"><div class="record"><div class="record-top"><span>ASSURANCE RECORD</span><b>VERIFIED</b></div><div class="record-title">Customer Support Agent <small>v4.2.1 · production</small></div><div class="record-grid"><div><label>IDENTITY</label><strong>VERIFIED</strong></div><div><label>AUTHORITY</label><strong>CONSTRAINED</strong></div><div><label>POLICY</label><strong>P-104</strong></div><div><label>DECISION</label><strong>ALLOW</strong></div><div><label>OUTCOME</label><strong>OBSERVED</strong></div><div><label>PROVENANCE</label><strong>BOUND</strong></div></div><div class="record-foot"><span>Evidence chain</span><span>System → Policy → Decision → Outcome</span></div></div><div class="evidence-list"><div><span>EV-0041</span><b>Policy snapshot</b><em>HASHED</em></div><div><span>EV-0042</span><b>Decision record</b><em>BOUND</em></div><div><span>EV-0043</span><b>Execution outcome</b><em>OBSERVED</em></div><div><span>EV-0044</span><b>Retest condition</b><em>READY</em></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section outcomes"><div class="outcome-panel"><div><div class="eyebrow">OPERATING OUTCOMES</div><h2>Make assurance operational, not documentary.</h2></div><div class="outcome-grid"><article><strong>01</strong><h3>Reduce uncontrolled actions</h3><p>Move authority decisions outside the model and into explicit, testable control boundaries.</p></article><article><strong>02</strong><h3>Shorten incident reconstruction</h3><p>Retain the context required to understand what acted, under which policy, and with what result.</p></article><article><strong>03</strong><h3>Support continuous reassessment</h3><p>Re-evaluate assurance when systems, models, tools, policies or material dependencies change.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="architecture" class="section architecture"><div class="section-head"><div class="eyebrow">TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE</div><h2>A control layer that sits between AI intent and consequential execution.</h2></div><div class="arch"><div class="arch-col"><span>01</span><b>AI SYSTEMS</b><small>Agents · models · workflows</small></div><div class="connector"></div><div class="arch-col featured"><span>02</span><b>AURELIS</b><small>Identity · policy · evidence · control</small></div><div class="connector"></div><div class="arch-col"><span>03</span><b>ENTERPRISE SYSTEMS</b><small>Data · tools · services · operations</small></div></div><div class="principles"><span>FAIL-CLOSED CONTROL</span><span>TENANT-SCOPED ACCESS</span><span>VERSION-BOUND EVIDENCE</span><span>DETERMINISTIC DECISIONS</span></div></section>
<section class="section final-cta"><div class="cta-box"><div class="eyebrow">BEGIN WITH ONE WORKFLOW</div><h2>Find the control boundary your AI system is missing.</h2><p>Describe the system, the actions it can take and the evidence you need to retain. Aurelis can then be evaluated against that boundary.</p><a class="button primary" href="/access.html">Request access ↗</a></div></section>
